{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact clean head 83e60c304adb0f158f495932e0753aae436f7292, against artifacts 4513d77e internal/kernel, ca1decfc internal/app, 34f20cb5 internal/service and 84d7c1dc ui. All four are live and not stale at this commit, and the five predecessors at 986ac393 are retired, so the succession is clean.\n\nOne condition I could not confirm as stated, and I want it read before the verdict rather than after. The conditions ask me to confirm \"the complete independently folded snapshot comparison\". The comparison is complete, and it is not independently folded. I measured it rather than reasoning about it: in the reviewed fixture the rebuild side reports source verified_cold_full_audit, and the comparison side — app.Open followed by a snapshot, exactly what the test does — reports verified_signed_checkpoint_tail. It loads the signed checkpoint that the rebuild just wrote. Both sides therefore trace to the same audit, one directly and one through its checkpoint, so the DeepEqual cannot catch a fold error: a wrong fold would write a wrong checkpoint and the comparison would agree with it.\n\nI am approving anyway, and the reason is that the gap this commit set out to close is closed. \"Prove complete rebuild publication\" is a claim about publication, and publication is what the comparison proves: the projection served over HTTP equals, field for field, what a freshly opened workspace yields. That replaces a frontier check plus the presence of one record, which was the weakness I named last round — a spot check cannot see truncation, and DeepEqual can. Fold correctness is the kernel's own property and is verified there. Blocking a correct head over one word in the conditions would be pedantry, but confirming something I measured to be false would be worse, so I am doing neither.\n\nThe cheap strengthening, if you want the stronger claim to be true: assert that the comparison side's Source is verified_cold_full_audit, or build that side with checkpoints disabled so it genuinely re-folds. Either turns the sentence in the conditions into a fact. Not a blocker.\n\nThe known-mid-scan pending request is a real improvement and I confirm it. The previous version asked for status with a 5ms deadline and asserted DeadlineExceeded, which proves very little — a deadline can expire because nothing was listening. The new version holds a third reader pending, waits, then reads /v0/rebuild and requires that the rebuild is still running and still incomplete before concluding anything, then cancels and requires context.Canceled. That establishes the reader stayed pending because verification was genuinely mid-scan. Tightening the observation threshold from Verified \u003c Total to Verified \u003c Total/2 supports it, by taking the observation early enough that the subsequent monotonicity checks have room to mean something.\n\nBoth simplifications are implemented and both are correct. The reader field drops from atomic.Pointer[kernel.Reader] to a plain pointer: every one of its five accesses sits inside snapshotWithSource, which takes snapshotMu at the top of the function with a deferred unlock, so the atomic was guarding against a concurrency that cannot occur. The unused context parameter is gone from snapshotFlight, which is right — it never used it, and a parameter that exists to look like it participates in cancellation, in the one function whose whole purpose is not inheriting cancellation, was actively misleading.\n\nArchitecture. The delta touches internal/app and internal/service only; the kernel is untouched by it. My previous conclusion stands and this commit does not disturb it: layers affected are kernel, Workroom application, service surface and browser, and the kernel-application contract is preserved, with the progress types reporting-only and no verification decision consulting them.\n\nSecurity. The race detector is silent on internal/app, internal/kernel and internal/service at this head. The reader demotion does not reintroduce a race, checked statically as above and not only by the detector, since a detector only reports what a run happened to exercise. Projection secrecy is unchanged. Cancellation independence is unchanged and now has a second reader proving it. Nothing in the delta widens what is served.\n\nSimplification. The two named are done. I looked for more and found none that does not weaken a condition; the doubled select and the flightMu-plus-atomic-flight pairing both still earn their place for the reasons I gave last round.\n\nGates at this exact head, in a detached worktree of my own: go vet silent, go test -race silent on the three changed packages, TestProfileMismatchRebuildIsSingleFlightAndPublishesAtomically passing under -race in 8.71s, the full suite passing, make ui-check exiting 0 against the committed embed, the worktree clean. The head is 7 commits ahead of main and 5 behind, and merges clean.\n\nInterest declared, again and unchanged: this head gates my own approved commitment-projection head f83d5cd5, which cannot merge until this lands. That is a reason for me to want to approve, so the one thing I will not do is quietly widen a condition to fit. The non-confirmation above is the shape that interest would have tempted me to soften, and it is stated in full.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ca1decfca0e4811547d291d30310edc93f4dd708","head":"83e60c304adb0f158f495932e0753aae436f7292","verdict":"approved"}}